      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looking into this some more,\n* Hal2AidlMapper::createOrUpdatePatch() when called with patchId 0 from framework is meant to create a new patch, but at the end of the method there is this code\n```\nif (existingPatchIt !\u003d mPatches.end()) {\n        RETURN_STATUS_IF_ERROR(statusTFromBinderStatus(\n                        mModule-\u003esetAudioPatch(patch, \u0026patch)));\n        existingPatchIt-\u003esecond \u003d patch;\n    } else {\n        bool created \u003d false;\n        RETURN_STATUS_IF_ERROR(findOrCreatePatch(patch, \u0026patch, \u0026created));\n        // No cleanup of the patch is needed, it is managed by the framework.\n        *patchId \u003d patch.id;\n        if (!created) {\n            // The framework might have \"created\" a patch which already existed due to\n            // stream creation. Need to release the ownership from the stream.\n            for (auto\u0026 s : mStreams) {\n                if (s.second.second \u003d\u003d patch.id) s.second.second \u003d -1;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n```\nIn the case of patchId 0 (existingPatchIt \u003d\u003d mPatches.end()), the else case is taken and findOrCreatePatch is called. In findOrCreatePatch, a patch exists based on different condition\n```\nauto patchIt \u003d findPatch(sourcePortConfigIds, sinkPortConfigIds);\n```\nand if the inner HAL patch was created during stream creation, then this patchIt will be found and no new patch will actually be created, which seems contradictory from the original patchId \u003d 0 framework request.\n\nIn the case of the 192kHz source device -\u003e 48 kHz sink device request, this doesn\u0027t end up causing a config mismatch error in remote submix, because the above path is taken, and the existing \"48 kHz -\u003e 48 kHz\" patch is found and the new \"192 kHz -\u003e 48 kHz\" patch does not have any effect.\n\nI\u0027m finding it difficult to reason about subsequent CLs like https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/frameworks/av/+/2909978/7 that are introducing regressions because of the baseline test results and implementation.",
      "parentUuid": "ca2693d1_99813cd5",
      "revId": "94b2bc8a2eac46f96bbb7da434d016681875cf6e",
